/* func_800A9ADC (ovl_town)  --  20 of 20 words, 3 DIFFERING, verdict SHAPE
   (advise.py) but the cause is ALLOCATION.  Parked 2026-11-04 by the s1104k
   group after 73 measured spellings and an 18-minute, 6-job permuter run that
   floored on this same 3.

   WHAT THE FUNCTION IS
   func_800A9B2C's (:27191) gate: a predicate over the two-byte descriptor view
   `b`, the same view func_8009B120 (:15313) tests with `p[1] == 0xD &&
   p[0] == 4`.  Kind (b[1]) 0xD passes variant (b[0]) 4 or 3; kind 1 passes
   anything but 8; every other kind passes.  First parameter dead, witnessed by
   the gap -- the body reads $a1 and never touches $a0, and func_800A9B2C calls
   it `func_800A9ADC(a, b)`.  `xori`/`sltiu 1` is this compiler's `== K`
   against a non-zero constant and `xori`/`sltu $zero` is its `!= K`;
   func_8009B120's comment records both.

   No frame, no jump table, no rodata of its own, NO relocations at all -- no
   `jal`, no %hi/%lo, no address-take.  seqcheck therefore has only the one
   intra-function `j` to check, and raw==relocdump cannot close while the
   candidate is wrong, so the `j` offset is compared against the listing by
   hand.

   THE RESIDUE, EXACTLY (candidate = the body at the bottom of this file)
     word 3   candidate `addiu $a0, $zero, 0x4`   target `nop`
     word 5   candidate `nop`                      target `addiu $v1, $zero, 0x4`
     word 6   candidate `beq $a1, $a0, .L..B24`    target `beq $a1, $v1, .L..B24`
   Every other word, including both `j`/`bne` offsets and the whole
   .L800A9B08 arm, is byte-identical.  The constant 4 is materialised in the
   WRONG BLOCK and therefore in the wrong register: the target emits it inside
   the 0xD arm, where it fills the `lbu $a1, 0x0($a1)` load-delay slot, and it
   gets $v1 (reusing b[1]'s register, dead on that path); the candidate emits
   it in the entry block, where `fill_simple_delay_slots` moves it into the
   first `bne`'s delay slot and $v1/$v0 are both taken so it gets $a0.

   THE MECHANISM, MEASURED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS
   1. The obvious spellings are 8 differing, not 3, and the extra cost is a
      trailing `addu $v0, $v1, $zero`.  `advise.py --greg` says why: with the
      comparison constant written as a LITERAL (`if (b[0] != 4)`), it is set
      once from a const_int, so local-alloc's `update_equiv_regs` gives it
      `reg_equiv_constant` and it is NOT AN ALLOCNO AT ALL -- it never appears
      in the .greg table.  reload then rematerialises it into the lowest free
      register, $v0, and the greg table reports $v0 as an OUTRIGHT CONFLICT for
      all four remaining pseudos, so the result pseudo can never have $v0 and
      the return copy survives.  No reference count or live-range change can
      beat an outright conflict; the MARGINS table's 20%/16.7% gaps are
      therefore irrelevant here, which is the documented "a margin is only
      meaningful where the formula decides" case.
   1b. THE CDK CITATION, which is the new mechanism here.
      scratch/gcc-src/cdk-gcc-b18/local-alloc.c:1043 is the gate --
      `|| reg_n_sets[regno] != 1` -- so the REG_EQUIV note, and therefore
      `reg_equiv_constant`, is recorded ONLY for a pseudo set exactly once.
      Then local-alloc.c:1071 says in its own words -- quoted WITHOUT its
      comment delimiters, because a nested `*` + `/` would close this block
      and turn every apostrophe below into an unterminated character
      constant, which is exactly how this file first failed parkstats:
        If this insn introduces a "constant" register, decrease the priority
        of that register.  ...
      and local-alloc.c:1105 does it:
              reg_live_length[regno] *= 2;
      guarded by the comment at :1103, "Note that the statement below does not
      affect the priority in local-alloc!" -- i.e. it is aimed at GLOBAL alloc.
      That doubling is visible in `advise.py --greg` for the k spelling: k is
      refs 2, live 14, priority 0.143, where the un-doubled live length is 7.
      So a `s32 k; k = <constant>;` local written as a statement of its own is
      an ALLOCATION-PRIORITY LEVER IN THE OPPOSITE DIRECTION from the known
      `do { } while (0)` one: it deliberately HALVES the constant's priority
      and hands the register to its rival -- here the result pseudo, which then
      wins $v0 and loses the copy.  The lever list has the priority-RAISING
      device; this is the priority-LOWERING counterpart, and it is the thing
      that moved this function 8 -> 3.
   2. Parking the constant in a LOCAL assigned ABOVE the `b[1]` test
      (`s32 k; k = 4; ... if (u != k)`) gives it two live blocks, so
      update_equiv_regs cannot fold it, it becomes a real global allocno, the
      $v0 conflict disappears, the result wins $v0, the `addu` goes away --
      8 -> 3 differing.  This is the whole 5-word gain.
   3. Moving that same `k = 4` INSIDE the arm puts the insn where the target
      has it but loses the allocation again (back to 8), because k is then
      confined to one basic block, update_equiv_regs folds it, and reload
      takes $v0.  A second set inside the arm (`k = 3` or `k = 0` in the inner
      arm) does not rescue it: still 8.
   4. Giving k its second set in the TAIL (`k = 1;` there, or reusing one
      variable for both arms' constants) fixes the allocation AND the insn's
      block, but costs 2 words somewhere else: cse stops forwarding the entry
      block's `lbu $v1, 0x1($a1)` into the tail and re-loads b[1].  21-24
      words, 15-20 differing.  THIS IS THE PLATEAU'S REAL WALL and the thing to
      attack next: the three-differing shape and the b[1]-forwarding shape are
      each reachable, and no spelling found reaches both.

   WHAT THIS CANDIDATE HOLDS FIXED (vary one of these next)
   * The function has exactly ONE basic block before the `b[1]` test.  Every
     spelling tried keeps b[1] loaded there.  Nothing tried moves the b[0] load
     up, or splits the entry block.
   * The tail is always one of two shapes -- `if (b[1] == 1) return b[0] != 8;
     return 1;` or its inverse -- both of which are byte-exact and were never
     varied beyond that, because words 11..19 match in every 3-differing
     candidate.
   * The dead first parameter is always `s32 a` and never read.  No spelling
     used it to create an entry-block allocno, which is precisely the kind of
     free global allocno point 2 needs.
   * No spelling made the pointer `b` anything but `u8 *`, so MEM_IN_STRUCT_P
     was never varied; the two `lbu`s are plain pointer dereferences in all 73.
   * The permuter ran from the 8-differing base, not from this 3-differing one.
     Its own best (score 15, an uninitialised-variable mutation) measures the
     same 3 differing, and its score-40 find measures 7.

   THE SPELLING TABLE is in the s1104k landing report.  Twenty-six spellings of
   the if/else, ternary, `||`-chain, switch, result-variable, `goto`-exit and
   `do { } while (0)` forms are all 8 or 9 differing at 20 words; the `||`
   first arm is 18 words; the single-result-variable-for-both-arms form is 19
   (its two `r = 1` unify and one `addiu` disappears). */
#include "common.h"

s32 func_800A9ADC(s32 a, u8 *b)
{
    s32 r;
    s32 u;
    s32 k;

    k = 4;
    if (b[1] == 0xD)
    {
        u = b[0];
        r = 1;
        if (u != k)
        {
            r = u == 3;
        }
        return r;
    }
    if (b[1] == 1)
    {
        return b[0] != 8;
    }
    return 1;
}
